summary:
In this article, we reanalyze the mass and pole residue of $\Lambda$-type singly heavy baryons with spin-parity $J^P=1/2^{\pm}$ using two-point QCD sum rules. Then, we investigate the electroweak transition form factors of $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)$ and $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)$ within the framework of three-point QCD sum rules. At the hadron side, all possible couplings of the interpolating currents to hadronic states are taken into account, while at the QCD side, both the perturbative part and vacuum condensate contributions up to dimension-8 are included. Using the obtained form factors, we calculate the decay widths and branching ratios for the semileptonic decays $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)\ell ar{
u}_\ell$ and $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)\ell ar{
u}_\ell$ ($\ell=e,\mu$ and $	au$), as well as for the corresponding nonleptonic decays $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)\pi[ho]$, $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)K[K^*]$, $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)\pi[ho]$ and $\Xi_b	o\Xi^*_c(2790)K[K^*]$. Our predictions for the branching ratios of $\Lambda_b	o\Lambda^*_c(2595)\ell ar{
u}_\ell$ are comparable with the experimental data and other theoretical results. In addition, we present predictions for several observables, including the lepton universality ratio, the forward-backward asymmetry $A_{FB}$, and the asymmetry parameter $\alpha$, which may be useful for future experimental tests. These results can provide valuable references for future measurements.

